 "measurementNotes": [
  "Baseline RMS is measured from a true mono decode (-ac 1): ffmpeg's mono->stereo upmix scales each channel by 0.707, so a -ac 2 decode under-reads a mono file by 3.01 dB. Grass RMS is the mono-fold (mean of channels) of a true stereo master -- the comparable figure for a cue played centred under an equal-power pan law.",
  "Guard-vs-parry LUFS comparison is conservative: a stereo render measures ~+3 LU over the same mono content (BS.1770 channel sum), so the real gap between the stereo guard drafts and the mono metal_parry is wider than the headline LUFS numbers show.",
  "Grass tonal prominence (400-2000 Hz) is recorded, not asserted: the cue's energy sits above 1800 Hz, so the median in 400-2000 Hz is near the noise floor and the ratio is not a tonality claim."
 ],
